<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<title>Cheques</title>
<style>
/* ============================================================================
   Three cheques per page
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Physical layout only. Every value is pre-formatted by the renderer, so this
   template can be edited from the Template admin surface without touching code.

   Geometry (Letter 215.9mm x 279.4mm):
     cheque 1      top      0mm .. 88.9mm   (8.5in x 3.5in)
     cheque 2      top   88.9mm .. 177.8mm
     cheque 3      top  177.8mm .. 266.7mm
     feed margin   top  266.7mm .. 279.4mm  (0.5in, nothing printed)
   MICR clear band = bottom 15.9mm (5/8in) of EACH cheque: nothing but the
   magnetic line may be printed there, or the reader rejects the item.

   There are no voucher stubs on this stock, so the payment reference and memo
   print on the cheque face itself - that is the only place left to carry them.

   This template iterates `Model.Pages`, NOT `Model.Checks`: the renderer has
   already grouped the batch into pages of `Model.ChecksPerPage`. The last page
   may hold fewer than three - the empty slots simply stay blank, they must not
   be filled with anything (a blank cheque form with a live MICR line is a
   negotiable instrument waiting to be written on).

   Pre-printed stock: the stock already carries the company/bank identity, the
   cheque number, the "$", "PAY TO THE ORDER OF", "DOLLARS" and the MICR line.
   Those elements carry Model.PrePrintedClass (= "noprint"), so they stay
   VISIBLE on screen (full simulation for proof-reading) and become
   visibility:hidden when printing - hidden but still occupying space.
   ========================================================================= */

@@page { size: auto; margin: 0; }

* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
    background: #eef0f3;
    font-family: Arial, "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, sans-serif;
    color: #000;
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
}

.cheque-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 215.9mm;
    height: 279.4mm;
    margin: 0 auto 8mm;
    background: #fff;
    box-shadow: 0 1mm 3mm rgba(0, 0, 0, .18);
    overflow: hidden;
    page-break-after: always;
}
.cheque-page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }

.abs { position: absolute; }

/* ---------- the three cheque bands ---------- */
.cheque { position: absolute; left: 0; width: 215.9mm; height: 88.9mm; }
.cheque.blank-stock { border-bottom: 0.3mm solid #444; }
.slot-1 { top: 0; }
.slot-2 { top: 88.9mm; }
.slot-3 { top: 177.8mm; }

/* Perforation guides between the bands (screen aid; they print faintly and stay
   clear of every MICR band because they sit exactly on a band boundary). */
.perforation { position: absolute; left: 0; width: 215.9mm; border-top: 0.2mm dashed #bbb; }
.perf-1 { top: 88.9mm; }
.perf-2 { top: 177.8mm; }
.feed-margin { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 266.7mm; width: 215.9mm; height: 12.7mm; }

.issuer { left: 10mm; top: 4mm; width: 92mm; }
.issuer-logo { max-height: 9mm; max-width: 38mm; display: block; margin-bottom: .8mm; }
.issuer-name { font-size: 10pt; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .2mm; }
.issuer-line { font-size: 6.5pt; line-height: 1.3; color: #222; }

/* Declared heights on the two top-right blocks are load-bearing, not decoration:
   the courtesy-amount clear area below is measured against them (see `.courtesy`).
   Three cheques to a sheet leaves 88.9mm per band, so this form is the tightest
   of the six - the top-right cluster moves up to buy the amount field its space. */
.cheque-no { right: 10mm; top: 4mm; width: 56mm; height: 4.5mm; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 700; }
.cheque-no-label { font-size: 6.5pt; font-weight: 400; color: #444; }

.date-block { right: 10mm; top: 9mm; width: 58mm; height: 8mm; text-align: right; }
.date-label { font-size: 6pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .4mm; color: #444; }
.date-value { font-size: 9.5pt; letter-spacing: .6mm; border-bottom: 0.25mm solid #000; padding-top: .5mm; }

.pay-label { left: 10mm; top: 28mm; font-size: 6pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .3mm; color: #333; }
.payee { left: 10mm; top: 31.5mm; width: 128mm; font-size: 10.5pt; font-weight: 700; border-bottom: 0.25mm solid #000; padding-bottom: .5mm; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }

/* ---- Courtesy amount ----
   A clear area around the amount field is what lets a reader isolate it. This
   layout is US 3-per-page stock and so is not governed by CPA-006, but its
   geometry was copied from the Canadian one and inherited the same too-tight
   numbers; the 6.4mm (0.25in) figure CPA-006 section 5.4.3 states is the only
   written dimension we have.

   Geometry (page is 215.9mm wide, band is 88.9mm tall):
     amount field 152.9mm .. 205.9mm   x   26mm .. 34.5mm   ("$" + box together)
     clear area   146.5mm .. 212.3mm   x   19.6mm .. 40.9mm
     above  .date-block  ends at 17mm    (needs <= 19.6mm)
     below  .legal       starts at 42mm  (needs >= 40.9mm)
     left   .payee       ends at 138mm   (needs <= 146.5mm)
   Nothing below the amount row moved: `.legal` at 42mm already cleared once the
   box came up, and the band has no room to push the lower half down. */
.courtesy { right: 10mm; top: 26mm; width: 48mm; height: 8.5mm; }
.courtesy-box { position: absolute; inset: 0; border: 0.3mm solid #000; }
.courtesy-sign { position: absolute; left: -5mm; top: 1.2mm; font-size: 10.5pt; font-weight: 700; }
.courtesy-value { position: absolute; right: 1.6mm; top: 1.4mm; font-size: 11.5pt; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }

.legal { left: 10mm; top: 42mm; width: 164mm; font-size: 9pt; border-bottom: 0.25mm solid #000; padding-bottom: .5mm; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }
.legal-currency { left: 176mm; top: 42mm; font-size: 7.5pt; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .2mm; }

.bank { left: 10mm; top: 49mm; width: 88mm; font-size: 7pt; line-height: 1.3; color: #222; }
.bank-name { font-weight: 700; font-size: 8pt; }

/* No stub on this stock, so the payment reference rides on the cheque face. */
.memo-label { left: 10mm; top: 62mm; font-size: 6pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .3mm; color: #333; }
.memo { left: 24mm; top: 61.5mm; width: 74mm; font-size: 7pt; border-bottom: 0.25mm solid #000; padding-bottom: .3mm; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }
.reference { left: 10mm; top: 66mm; width: 88mm; font-size: 6.5pt; color: #555; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }

.signature { left: 128mm; top: 50mm; width: 78mm; }
.signature-image { height: 8mm; display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center; }
.signature-image img { max-height: 8mm; max-width: 68mm; }
.signature-line { border-top: 0.25mm solid #000; margin-top: .4mm; }
.signature-name { font-size: 7pt; text-align: center; padding-top: .3mm; }
.signature-title { font-size: 6pt; text-align: center; color: #333; }

.micr-band { left: 0; bottom: 0; width: 215.9mm; height: 15.9mm; }
.micr-line { position: absolute; left: 32mm; bottom: 5mm; font-family: "MICR E13B", "E-13B", "GnuMICR", monospace; font-size: 12pt; letter-spacing: .5mm; white-space: nowrap; }
.micr-readable { position: absolute; left: 32mm; bottom: 1.2mm; font-size: 5.5pt; letter-spacing: .4mm; color: #555; white-space: nowrap; }

.preview-watermark {
    left: 0; top: 26mm; width: 215.9mm;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 22pt;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 1.6mm;
    color: rgba(190, 30, 45, .22);
    transform: rotate(-8deg);
    pointer-events: none;
}

@@media print {
    body { background: #fff; }
    .cheque-page { margin: 0; box-shadow: none; }
    /* Pre-printed stock: keep the space, drop the ink. */
    .noprint { visibility: hidden; }
}

/* ---------- specimen mode (layout picker) ----------
   A specimen is rendered from placeholder data so somebody choosing a layout
   can hold it against the paper in the printer. The question it has to answer
   is "what does this layout put on MY stock", and on pre-printed stock the
   answer is "the elements below are already there - the printer only adds the
   variable data".

   `.noprint` alone cannot say that: it lives inside @@media print, so on screen
   those elements render exactly as they do on blank stock, and the two stock
   types look the same in a thumbnail. Fading them is the signal that survives
   on screen and at thumbnail scale. One knob - change the opacity, or swap it
   for a grayscale/dashed treatment, whatever reads best on your stock.

   Scoped under `.specimen`, which only a specimen puts on the page root: a real
   cheque and a payment preview match nothing here, so their output is
   untouched (a preview SHOULD show the full face - you are proof-reading a
   cheque then, not comparing paper). */
.specimen .noprint { opacity: .28; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
@foreach (var page in Model.Pages)
{
    @* The ternary supplies its own leading space, so a real cheque still renders
       exactly `class="cheque-page"` - byte-identical to before specimen mode. *@
    <section class="cheque-page@(Model.IsSpecimen ? " specimen" : "")" style="@Model.OffsetStyle">

        <div class="perforation perf-1"></div>
        <div class="perforation perf-2"></div>
        <div class="feed-margin"></div>

        @for (var slot = 0; slot < page.Checks.Count; slot++)
        {
            var chk = page.Checks[slot];
            <div class="cheque slot-@(slot + 1) @(Model.IsPrePrinted ? "" : "blank-stock")">

                @if (Model.IsPreview)
                {
                    <div class="abs preview-watermark">@Model.PreviewLabel</div>
                }

                @if (Model.Issuer.HasIdentity)
                {
                    <div class="abs issuer @Model.PrePrintedClass">
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.Issuer.LogoUrl))
                        {
                            <img class="issuer-logo" src="@Model.Issuer.LogoUrl" alt="" />
                        }
                        <div class="issuer-name">@Model.Issuer.Name</div>
                        @foreach (var line in Model.Issuer.AddressLines)
                        {
                            <div class="issuer-line">@line</div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }

                <div class="abs cheque-no @Model.PrePrintedClass">
                    <span class="cheque-no-label">No.</span> @chk.CheckNumberText
                </div>

                @* ISO date: unambiguous however it is read, and the framework must not
                   guess a national date order. *@
                <div class="abs date-block">
                    <div class="date-label @Model.PrePrintedClass">Date</div>
                    <div class="date-value">@chk.IssueDateIso</div>
                </div>

                <div class="abs pay-label @Model.PrePrintedClass">Pay to the order of</div>
                <div class="abs payee">@chk.PayeeName</div>

                <div class="abs courtesy">
                    <div class="courtesy-box @Model.PrePrintedClass"></div>
                    <div class="courtesy-sign @Model.PrePrintedClass">$</div>
                    <div class="courtesy-value">@chk.AmountText</div>
                </div>

                <div class="abs legal">@chk.AmountInWordsText</div>
                <div class="abs legal-currency @Model.PrePrintedClass">@chk.CurrencyLabel</div>

                <div class="abs bank @Model.PrePrintedClass">
                    <div class="bank-name">@Model.Bank.Name</div>
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.Bank.RoutingLine))
                    {
                        <div>@Model.Bank.RoutingLine</div>
                    }
                </div>

                <div class="abs memo-label @Model.PrePrintedClass">Memo</div>
                <div class="abs memo">@chk.Memo</div>
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(chk.PaymentNumber) || !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(chk.Reference))
                {
                    <div class="abs reference">@chk.PaymentNumber @chk.Reference</div>
                }

                <div class="abs signature">
                    <div class="signature-image">
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.Issuer.SignatureImageUrl))
                        {
                            <img src="@Model.Issuer.SignatureImageUrl" alt="" />
                        }
                    </div>
                    <div class="signature-line @Model.PrePrintedClass"></div>
                    <div class="signature-name">@Model.Issuer.SignatureName</div>
                    <div class="signature-title">@Model.Issuer.SignatureTitle</div>
                </div>

                <div class="abs micr-band">
                    @if (Model.ShowMicr)
                    {
                        <div class="micr-line">@chk.MicrGlyphs</div>
                        <div class="micr-readable">@chk.MicrLine</div>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        }

    </section>
}
</body>
</html>
